From: djnice <djnice77@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] GraphicContext: no GUI resize broadcast when the mode did not
 change

On Amlogic every SetVideoResolution is forced, so PlaybackCleanup after a
windowed video (a background trailer) re-applies the unchanged GUI mode and
broadcasts GUI_MSG_WINDOW_RESIZE. That frees every large texture and reloads
the fonts for nothing: one near-black frame and a visible redraw of the whole
GUI each time a trailer stops. The broadcast is now sent only when the GUI
geometry (GUI and screen size, pixel ratio, overscan, insets, subtitle line,
stereo flags) really changed.

Measured on S928X with the VPP output read back by VDIN1: leaving an info
screen with a playing trailer showed a frame at mean luma 18 between two at
84; with the patch the transition has no such frame.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 xbmc/windowing/GraphicContext.cpp | 27 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/GraphicContext.cpp b/xbmc/windowing/GraphicContext.cpp
index 0249ce4403..ee45faf96e 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/GraphicContext.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/GraphicContext.cpp
@@ -445,6 +445,9 @@ void CGraphicContext::SetVideoResolutionInternal(RESOLUTION res, bool forceUpdat
   int origScreenWidth = m_iScreenWidth;
   int origScreenHeight = m_iScreenHeight;
   float origFPSOverride = m_fFPSOverride;
+  const bool lastResValid = IsValidResolution(lastRes);
+  const RESOLUTION_INFO lastInfo =
+      lastResValid ? CDisplaySettings::GetInstance().GetResolutionInfo(lastRes) : RESOLUTION_INFO();
 
   UpdateInternalStateWithResolution(res);
   RESOLUTION_INFO info_org  = CDisplaySettings::GetInstance().GetResolutionInfo(res);
@@ -478,8 +481,30 @@ void CGraphicContext::SetVideoResolutionInternal(RESOLUTION res, bool forceUpdat
     // update anyone that relies on sizing information
     CServiceBroker::GetInputManager().SetMouseResolution(info_org.iWidth, info_org.iHeight, 1, 1);
 
+    // A forced re-apply of an unchanged mode (on Amlogic every update is forced, e.g. the
+    // PlaybackCleanup after a windowed trailer) leaves the GUI geometry as it was. The resize
+    // broadcast would free every large texture and reload the fonts for nothing: one
+    // near-black frame and a visible redraw of the whole GUI.
+    const RESOLUTION_INFO newInfo = CDisplaySettings::GetInstance().GetResolutionInfo(res);
+    const bool geometryChanged =
+        !lastResValid || lastInfo.iWidth != newInfo.iWidth ||
+        lastInfo.iHeight != newInfo.iHeight || lastInfo.iScreenWidth != newInfo.iScreenWidth ||
+        lastInfo.iScreenHeight != newInfo.iScreenHeight ||
+        lastInfo.iBlanking != newInfo.iBlanking || lastInfo.iSubtitles != newInfo.iSubtitles ||
+        lastInfo.fPixelRatio != newInfo.fPixelRatio ||
+        lastInfo.Overscan.left != newInfo.Overscan.left ||
+        lastInfo.Overscan.top != newInfo.Overscan.top ||
+        lastInfo.Overscan.right != newInfo.Overscan.right ||
+        lastInfo.Overscan.bottom != newInfo.Overscan.bottom ||
+        lastInfo.guiInsets.left != newInfo.guiInsets.left ||
+        lastInfo.guiInsets.top != newInfo.guiInsets.top ||
+        lastInfo.guiInsets.right != newInfo.guiInsets.right ||
+        lastInfo.guiInsets.bottom != newInfo.guiInsets.bottom ||
+        (lastInfo.dwFlags & D3DPRESENTFLAG_MODEMASK) != (newInfo.dwFlags & D3DPRESENTFLAG_MODEMASK) ||
+        origScreenWidth != m_iScreenWidth || origScreenHeight != m_iScreenHeight;
+
     CGUIComponent *gui = CServiceBroker::GetGUI();
-    if (gui)
+    if (gui && geometryChanged)
       gui->GetWindowManager().SendMessage(GUI_MSG_NOTIFY_ALL, 0, 0, GUI_MSG_WINDOW_RESIZE);
   }
   else
